# Taken-edge asm-goto outputs are an lccc extension: no reference compiler
# defines an output object on an edge taken by the template's own branch.
# Measured on this fixture's shapes: gcc 12 answers f(0) with the fall-through
# path at -O0 and with the label path at -O2, and clang 22 returns 101 at -O0
# versus 244 at -O2 for the same flag read -- each compiler disagrees with
# itself, so the fixture cannot assert a portable value and the oracle fails
# its own assertions by construction. lccc materialises outputs on every edge;
# that stronger guarantee is what this file pins. The portable half of the same
# coverage lives in asm_goto_outputs.c, which passes on gcc and clang at -O0
# and -O2.
LCCC_ORACLE_SELFCHECK=skip
